# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tests of a sanitized build
# (ALAddTestBinary.cmake gives the runs this file), and for runs of its
# viewer. One per line:
#
#   race:<function or source file>
#   called_from_lib:<library>
#   deadlock:<function>
#
# A suppression is for code that is not ours and that the tsan triplet cannot
# build instrumented, such as the system's GL driver under the gl tests, and
# says above it what it hides, why it cannot be fixed here, and where it was
# reported upstream. A race in our own code is fixed, not listed, and one in
# a port the Alchemy registry carries is patched there.

# Mesa's llvmpipe, the GL the gl tests run on in CI and on a host without a
# GPU: libgallium, built by the distribution, uninstrumented. Its threads
# order their work through futexes TSan cannot see, so each time Mesa
# destroyed a mutex or condition variable an llvmpipe thread had used, TSan
# reported a race between the two, from Mesa on both sides: 49 reports in
# the gl tests of one run. This hides a race with Mesa in either stack.
# called_from_lib, which would have TSan ignore what Mesa calls instead,
# leaves it half of Mesa's locking to see: it then reports lock-order
# inversions through the LLVM llvmpipe compiles with, and runs hang. Not a
# bug to report: Mesa is not built for TSan.
race:libgallium

# SDL's PipeWire audio backend, from the Alchemy registry's sdl3: a
# lock-order inversion between a device's lock and its stream's PipeWire
# loop lock, which cannot deadlock. OpenPhysicalAudioDevice holds the
# device lock while PIPEWIRE_OpenDevice takes the loop lock, and the loop's
# thread, holding the loop lock, calls output_callback, which takes the
# device lock. Each device has a loop of its own, and output_callback takes
# the device lock only once the open has set PW_READY_FLAG_OPEN_COMPLETE
# under the loop lock, writing silence until then; closing a device lets
# its lock go before it stops the loop. So the one order is over before
# the other begins, a protocol TSan's lock graph cannot see. Not patched:
# SDL's locking is right, and a patch would only hide it from TSan.
deadlock:SDL_pipewire.c
